{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502567-mta-the-victorian-age","id":1502567,"title":"MTA The Victorian Age?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-08T19:11:31-08:00","id":1502567,"title":"MTA The Victorian Age?","content":"Do any of the published books deal directly with the events of the Victorian Age, did I miss something?<br /> Given the Nameless War, Great Refusal and the formation of a new Pentacle (and I would suspect a restructuring of the Seer Ministries) I would think this time period would have has much to offer Awakening as it does the Ascension, yet even in the Dark Eras books and Companion the only Mage related setting seems to be Mysterious Frontiers which takes place in the American West and points out that neither the Diamond nor Seers are firmly established there leaving it a truly wild frontier.<br /> I purchased the M20 pdf (and then a week later it went on sale for half price...dang) and I can see a lot of inspiration that can be taken from it, but I can't help but think there should be a resource for the Awakening directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T20:46:56-08:00","id":1502579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502567-mta-the-victorian-age#post1502567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do any of the published books deal directly with the events of the Victorian Age, did I miss something?<br /> Given the Nameless War, Great Refusal and the formation of a new Pentacle (and I would suspect a restructuring of the Seer Ministries) I would think this time period would have has much to offer Awakening as it does the Ascension, yet even in the Dark Eras books and Companion the only Mage related setting seems to be Mysterious Frontiers which takes place in the American West and points out that neither the Diamond nor Seers are firmly established there leaving it a truly wild frontier.<br /> I purchased the M20 pdf (and then a week later it went on sale for half price...dang) and I can see a lot of inspiration that can be taken from it, but I can't help but think there should be a resource for the Awakening directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, none of 1e's books are set in the Victorian Period, and 2e doesn't really have a lot in the way of setting books.<br /> <br /> The Great Refusal happened right at the end of that era -the logistics of which, at least in the sweeping terms it's usually described in, boggles the mind- so there isn't a huge reason to have a specific setting dedicated to it any more than any other era. It's an interesting event, certainly, but my personal opinion is that it's one of those metaplot-y periods that don't jive well with Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T13:44:46-08:00","id":1502637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502567-mta-the-victorian-age#post1502567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do any of the published books deal directly with the events of the Victorian Age, did I miss something?<br /> Given the Nameless War, Great Refusal and the formation of a new Pentacle (and I would suspect a restructuring of the Seer Ministries) I would think this time period would have has much to offer Awakening as it does the Ascension, yet even in the Dark Eras books and Companion the only Mage related setting seems to be Mysterious Frontiers which takes place in the American West and points out that neither the Diamond nor Seers are firmly established there leaving it a truly wild frontier.<br /> I purchased the M20 pdf (and then a week later it went on sale for half price...dang) and I can see a lot of inspiration that can be taken from it, but I can't help but think there should be a resource for the Awakening directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that the events of The Devil and the Deep Blue Sea technically demarcate the earliest conflict of the Nameless War-sure, it's not called that at that point, but with the dissolution of the Company of the Codex comes the diaspora of their ideals, which leads to the development of the coalition of Nameless Orders that the the Pentacle are warring with.<br /> <br /> Anyways, THe Free Council book <i>should</i> cover details and major events for it. If not....Well, we still don't have Mage Camelot either, so maybe a book of particular eras for Mage would be an idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T02:59:36-08:00","id":1503609,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474433-tome-of-the-pentacle-release-date\"><b>Tome of Pentacle</b></a> should gone much in to Nameless War events - in truth, it both separated and build modern Pentacle alliance. It both highlights differences of Free Council to Diamond Orders - and also they reasons why they allied against Seers of Throne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}